hadiths[3]{hadithnumber,text}:
"15846","Yazid narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Said informed us that Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Habban informed him that his uncle Abu Sirmah used to narrate that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to say: O Allah, I ask You my sufficiency and the sufficiency of my freed slave."
"15847","Qutaybah ibn Said narrated to us: Layth narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Said, from Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Habban, from Luluah, from Abu Sirmah, from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, that he said: Whoever causes harm, Allah will harm him, and whoever causes hardship, Allah will cause hardship upon him."
"15848","Qutaybah ibn Said narrated to us, he said: Layth narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Said, from Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Habban, from Luluah, from Abu Sirmah, from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, that he said: O Allah, I ask You my sufficiency and the sufficiency of my freed slave."
